{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"center_ai_dc","type":"text","text":"# AI Data Center Industry\n\nDemand -> Product -> System -> Physical -> Capital\n\n[[Framework - How to look at this industry]]","x":-120,"y":-70,"width":300,"height":230,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"layer5","type":"text","text":"## Layer 5: Capital & Timeline\n\nWho pays, when revenue starts, and what can break?\n\n[[Layer 5 - Capital and timeline]]","x":-760,"y":330,"width":320,"height":195,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"enterprise_stages","type":"text","text":"### Enterprise Adoption\n\nExperiment -> Adoption -> Workflow transformation\n\nStable datacenter demand appears when AI enters production workflows.","x":-1320,"y":-220,"width":300,"height":230},
		{"id":"layer1","type":"text","text":"## Layer 1: AI Demand\n\nWhy is compute needed?\n\n[[Layer 1 - AI Demand (Application, model, inference, enterprise procurement)]]","x":-760,"y":-495,"width":300,"height":185,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"capital_capex","type":"text","text":"### Capex\n\nGPUs, servers, networking, storage, power, cooling, land, building, commissioning\n\n[[Layer 5 - Capital and timeline#1. What capex actually includes|What capex includes]]","x":-1320,"y":683,"width":300,"height":195},
		{"id":"capital_revenue","type":"text","text":"### Revenue & Utilization\n\nCapacity only matters if sold, used, paid for, and renewed.\n\n[[Layer 5 - Capital and timeline#Module 2: Revenue & Utilization|Revenue & Utilization]]","x":-1320,"y":480,"width":300,"height":150},
		{"id":"capital_timeline","type":"text","text":"### Timeline\n\nContract -> power -> build -> equipment -> commissioning -> revenue ramp\n\n[[Layer 5 - Capital and timeline#1. The timeline from capex to revenue|Timeline]]","x":-1320,"y":245,"width":300,"height":198},
		{"id":"capital_risk","type":"text","text":"### Risk Waterfall\n\nPower, construction, supply chain, commissioning, demand, utilization, pricing, obsolescence, financing\n\n[[Layer 5 - Capital and timeline#6. Risk waterfall|Risk waterfall]]","x":-1320,"y":30,"width":300,"height":200},
		{"id":"cross_chain","type":"text","text":"## Core Conversion Chain\n\nAI usage -> tokens / GPU-hours -> workloads -> useful compute -> physical capacity -> paid utilization -> cash flow","x":-210,"y":-847,"width":420,"height":170},
		{"id":"physical_metrics","type":"text","text":"### Physical Metrics\n\nMW, PUE, WUE, kW/rack, cooling capacity, time to power, uptime, electricity cost\n\n[[Layer 4 - Physical#Module 6: Physical Metrics / Unit Economics Bridge|Physical Metrics]]","x":-300,"y":910,"width":300,"height":180},
		{"id":"physical_site","type":"text","text":"### Site Selection\n\nPower-first, then land, fiber, water, policy, customer fit.\n\n[[Layer 4 - Physical#Module 3: Site / Land / Grid Access|Site / Grid Access]]","x":60,"y":910,"width":300,"height":150},
		{"id":"physical_cooling","type":"text","text":"### Cooling\n\nAir, rear-door, direct-to-chip, immersion, CDU, chiller, dry cooler\n\n[[Layer 4 - Physical#Module 2: Cooling / Thermal System|Cooling / Thermal System]]","x":420,"y":910,"width":300,"height":150},
		{"id":"physical_power","type":"text","text":"### Power Chain\n\nGrid -> substation -> transformer -> switchgear -> UPS -> rack power\n\n[[Layer 4 - Physical#Module 1: Electricity / Power Chain|Electricity / Power Chain]]","x":770,"y":910,"width":300,"height":180},
		{"id":"system_software","type":"text","text":"### Software / Scheduler\n\nSoftware turns theoretical compute into useful compute.\n\nKey: batching, KV cache, scheduler, observability\n\n[[Layer 3 - Computing System#Module 6: Software Stack|Software Stack]]","x":1240,"y":760,"width":300,"height":225},
		{"id":"system_network","type":"text","text":"### Network\n\nScale-up: inside server / rack\n\nScale-out: between servers / racks\n\n[[Layer 3 - Computing System#Module 4：Network|Network]]","x":1240,"y":505,"width":300,"height":180},
		{"id":"system_workload","type":"text","text":"### Workloads\n\nTraining turns data + compute into models.\n\nInference turns models into token / API revenue.\n\n[[Layer 3 - Computing System#Module 1: Workload|Workload]]","x":1240,"y":10,"width":300,"height":220},
		{"id":"system_chip","type":"text","text":"### Chip / Accelerator\n\nFLOPS + HBM + interconnect + power efficiency + software ecosystem\n\n[[Layer 3 - Computing System#Module 2: Chip/Accelerator|Chip / Accelerator]]","x":1240,"y":282,"width":300,"height":198},
		{"id":"layer3","type":"text","text":"## Layer 3: Computing System\n\nWhat produces useful compute?\n\n[[Layer 3 - Computing System]]","x":440,"y":165,"width":300,"height":165,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"product_surfaces","type":"text","text":"### Product Surfaces\n\n- Token API\n- Cloud AI service\n- GPU cloud\n- Enterprise AI platform\n- Managed AI supercomputing\n\n[[Layer 2 - Computing product#2. Product Types in Detail|Product types]]","x":1240,"y":-270,"width":300,"height":250},
		{"id":"product_risk_allocation","type":"text","text":"### Risk Allocation\n\nWho bears utilization risk?\n\n- Customer\n- Cloud platform\n- GPU cloud\n- Data center operator\n\n[[Layer 2 - Computing product#1.2 By risk allocation|By risk allocation]]","x":1240,"y":-560,"width":300,"height":260},
		{"id":"product_revenue_units","type":"text","text":"### Revenue Units\n\n- Token / API\n- GPU-hour\n- Reserved capacity\n- Provisioned throughput\n- MW lease\n\n[[Layer 2 - Computing product#1.3 By revenue unit|By revenue unit]]","x":1240,"y":-909,"width":300,"height":295},
		{"id":"layer2","type":"text","text":"## Layer 2: Computing Product\n\nHow is compute sold?\n\n[[Layer 2 - Computing product]]","x":570,"y":-485,"width":300,"height":185,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"players_supply","type":"text","text":"### Supply-Side Players\n\n- NVIDIA / AMD / Intel\n- Broadcom / Marvell / Arista\n- Dell / HPE / Supermicro / ODMs\n- Schneider / Vertiv / Eaton\n- Colo / hyperscalers / neoclouds","x":-570,"y":-801,"width":300,"height":248},
		{"id":"players_demand","type":"text","text":"### Demand-Side Players\n\n- Model labs\n- Hyperscalers\n- Enterprises\n- Developers\n- Sovereign AI\n- Consumer AI apps","x":290,"y":-847,"width":300,"height":238},
		{"id":"layer4","type":"text","text":"## Layer 4: Physical\n\nWhat constrains deployment?\n\n[[Layer 4 - Physical]]","x":360,"y":505,"width":320,"height":140,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"questions","type":"text","text":"## Questions To Ask\n\n1. Is demand training-driven or inference-driven?\n2. Is revenue usage-based or contracted?\n3. Who bears utilization risk?\n4. Is power secured or just requested?\n5. Can the system be delivered before pricing changes?\n6. Does contract duration exceed GPU payback risk?","x":-970,"y":860,"width":420,"height":300},
		{"id":"metrics_bridge","type":"text","text":"## Metrics Bridge\n\n- MFU: chip/system efficiency\n- GPU utilization: capacity use\n- PUE: facility efficiency\n- Revenue/MW: asset efficiency\n- Cost/token: service economics","x":-510,"y":595,"width":420,"height":221},
		{"id":"demand_quality","type":"text","text":"### Demand Quality\n\nHigh-quality demand is frequent, paid, workflow-embedded, SLA-backed, and predictable.\n\n[[Layer 1 - AI Demand (Application, model, inference, enterprise procurement)#Demand Quality Scoring|Demand Quality Scoring]]","x":-1320,"y":-462,"width":300,"height":210},
		{"id":"demand_types","type":"text","text":"### Demand Types\n\n- Frontier training\n- Inference\n- Enterprise workflow\n- Agent / tool-use\n\n[[Layer 1 - AI Demand (Application, model, inference, enterprise procurement)#Four demand types for AI:|Four demand types]]","x":-1320,"y":-700,"width":300,"height":215}
